{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BW684APRBxKxuWFqgdLFx2","type":"tool_result","content":"==> docs/agent-ops/INTAKE_RECORD.md <==\n# Intake Record — S0\n\n- Intake ID: WRK-2026-10-23-platform\n- Date: 2026-10-23\n- Requested by / owner: founder\n- Status: CONFIRMED\n- Lane: normal\n\n## 1. Request (verbatim)\n\n> \"I want to build an enterprise work-management platform with ERP and mobile. Where do we start?\"\n\n## 2. Deliverables and classes\n\n| ID | Deliverable | Files/modules inspected | Class | Validation floor | Reviewers | Owner approval before work? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | A new platform (\"Worklane\"), separate from Ledgerly; Ledgerly's invoicing may later become its billing module | repository (only Ledgerly exists) | platform (new) | discovery, brief, roadmap | product, architecture | Yes (given 2026-10-23) |\n\n## 3. Duplicate and conflict check\n\nNEW: no record of a work-management platform. Ledgerly (`decisions/ADR-0001-modular-monolith.md`) is related only as a possible billing module.\n\n## 4. Intent and value (owner-confirmed)\n\n- Problem: mid-size companies run projects, purchasing and invoicing in separate tools.\n- Owner confirmation: founder, 2026-10-23, \"Confirmed. Start with platform discovery; no metrics agreed yet.\"\n\n## 5. Scope contract\n\n- Next gate: /platform-discovery. No code in this phase.\n\n==> decisions/ADR-0001-modular-monolith.md <==\n# ADR-0001: Modular monolith\n\n- Status: DECIDED\n- Date: 2026-09-01\n- Decision owner: Product owner\n\n## Decision\nLedgerly stays a single Node service with modules per domain (invoices, payments) until load or team size justifies separation.\n\n## Rejected\nMicroservices per domain: operational cost not justified for one small team.\n\n==> projects/demo/PRD.md <==\n# PRD: Billing area\n\n## Problem\nFinance staff rebuild invoice lists by hand in spreadsheets every month.\n\n## Users\nFinance staff and organization admins.\n\n## Requirements\n- R1: Users can see all invoices of their own organization, never another organization's.\n- R2: Only admins can void an invoice.\n- R3: Exports include all historical invoices for the organization.\n- R4: Invoice totals are shown in the organization's currency.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Payments collection in this phase.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e3fcf44-9122-45b5-9b2b-7d67d834e7d4","uuid":"24638225-7a75-46dc-94b0-2d440956deb6","timestamp":"2026-11-11T00:30:56.619Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"==> docs/agent-ops/INTAKE_RECORD.md <==\n# Intake Record — S0\n\n- Intake ID: WRK-2026-10-23-platform\n- Date: 2026-10-23\n- Requested by / owner: founder\n- Status: CONFIRMED\n- Lane: normal\n\n## 1. Request (verbatim)\n\n> \"I want to build an enterprise work-management platform with ERP and mobile. Where do we start?\"\n\n## 2. Deliverables and classes\n\n| ID | Deliverable | Files/modules inspected | Class | Validation floor | Reviewers | Owner approval before work? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 | A new platform (\"Worklane\"), separate from Ledgerly; Ledgerly's invoicing may later become its billing module | repository (only Ledgerly exists) | platform (new) | discovery, brief, roadmap | product, architecture | Yes (given 2026-10-23) |\n\n## 3. Duplicate and conflict check\n\nNEW: no record of a work-management platform. Ledgerly (`decisions/ADR-0001-modular-monolith.md`) is related only as a possible billing module.\n\n## 4. Intent and value (owner-confirmed)\n\n- Problem: mid-size companies run projects, purchasing and invoicing in separate tools.\n- Owner confirmation: founder, 2026-10-23, \"Confirmed. Start with platform discovery; no metrics agreed yet.\"\n\n## 5. Scope contract\n\n- Next gate: /platform-discovery. No code in this phase.\n\n==> decisions/ADR-0001-modular-monolith.md <==\n# ADR-0001: Modular monolith\n\n- Status: DECIDED\n- Date: 2026-09-01\n- Decision owner: Product owner\n\n## Decision\nLedgerly stays a single Node service with modules per domain (invoices, payments) until load or team size justifies separation.\n\n## Rejected\nMicroservices per domain: operational cost not justified for one small team.\n\n==> projects/demo/PRD.md <==\n# PRD: Billing area\n\n## Problem\nFinance staff rebuild invoice lists by hand in spreadsheets every month.\n\n## Users\nFinance staff and organization admins.\n\n## Requirements\n- R1: Users can see all invoices of their own organization, never another organization's.\n- R2: Only admins can void an invoice.\n- R3: Exports include all historical invoices for the organization.\n- R4: Invoice totals are shown in the organization's currency.\n\n## Non-goals\n- Payments collection in this phase.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BW684APRBxKxuWFqgdLFx2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
